#reason src/main/diagnostics/editor.ts Failures inside the editor page need their own mapping so harmless VS Code noise and the token never reach the log.
#reason test/diagnostics-editor.test.ts Proves mapping, noise filter, token redaction, severity, throttle and freeze handling.
#reason docs/diagnostics.md Tells people editor entries exist and how to show them.
#reason src/main/diagnostics/capture.ts The existing hook for new windows is where the editor webview is attached, so no second window-level hack is needed.
#reason src/main/diagnostics/ipc.ts Whole-log reports must not be flooded by hidden editor warnings, yet a chosen entry stays reportable.
#reason src/preload/workspace.ts The window passes the editor choice along with the report request.
#reason src/renderer/diagnostics.css Styles the new checkbox in the toolbar.
#reason src/renderer/features/diagnostics.ts Forwards the editor checkbox choice to copy and GitHub reports.
#reason src/renderer/global.d.ts Types the extra report option for the window.
#reason src/renderer/lib/diagnostics-model.ts Decides which entries the list shows, hiding quiet editor ones by default.
#reason src/renderer/lib/diagnosticsview.ts Adds the checkbox that reveals editor console warnings and keeps counts and reports in step with it.
#reason src/shared/diagnostics.ts The new source, its label and the rule for what is quiet are shared by the log, reports and the view.
#reason test/diagnostics-github.test.ts Proves whole-log reports leave out quiet editor entries unless asked.
#reason test/diagnostics-view.test.ts Proves editor warnings are hidden by default and the checkbox reaches the report.
#story Errors inside the editor are logged
#step actor The editor page
#step action reports an error, fails to load or freezes
#step subject the Diagnostics log
#file src/main/diagnostics/editor.ts
#file src/main/diagnostics/capture.ts
#file test/diagnostics-editor.test.ts
#below interaction Open Diagnostics to see what went wrong in the editor
#file src/renderer/lib/diagnosticsview.ts
#below consequence Editor errors left no trace => They appear as Editor entries, token removed
#story Editor noise stays out of the way
#step actor A person
#step action opens Diagnostics or copies a report
#step subject the list and the report
#file src/renderer/lib/diagnostics-model.ts
#file src/main/diagnostics/ipc.ts
#file test/diagnostics-view.test.ts
#below interaction Tick Editor console warnings to include them
#below consequence Everything recorded filled the list => Editor warnings are hidden until asked for
